<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/012eb9ed5ab0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[364] Navinder Singh Sarao was eventually convicted for his role in the 2010 flash crash, as he used a spoofing algorithm to cause the crash." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "364" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0b5172c8fa8d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[370] A single selling order of an enormously large amount of E-Mini S&P contracts and subsequent aggressive selling orders executed by high-frequency algorithms triggered the massive decline in market prices." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "370" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0cde3903ad5f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Trading systems were reactivated and liquidity was restored." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "348" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0e054c6366bd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "But he had to keep constantly updating his orders to keep them a few ticks higher than the best offer, to make sure that he didn't accidentally sell any futures as the market moved. And that's a bit of a pain, so he programmed an algorithm to do it for him." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "346" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0e86037e025a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Each purchase introduced additional market exposure and risk, prompting these trading programs to hedge their own risk by selling these same futures." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "348" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1d0c5bcb01ae> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Sarao used the E-mini S&P 500 contract to conduct spoofing, the court document says." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "350" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1d2c45ebf5d9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[345] On April 21, 2015, nearly five years after the incident, the U.S. Department of Justice laid \"22 criminal counts, including fraud and market manipulation\" against Navinder Singh Sarao, a trader." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "345" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/26099ad6d7af> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Guy Trading at Home Caused the Flash Crash" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "346" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2936174739e1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "According to the report, many of the firms that bought the initial batch of futures from Waddell & Reed used automated trading software." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "348" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2cf249f4091e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "He faces 22 charges in the US, including fraud charges, all of which he denies - which include \"spoofing\" - the practice of buying or selling with the intent to cancel the transaction before execution." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "363" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2e01de08ff5f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "As reflected in correspondence with both SARAO and an FCM he used, the CME observed that, between September 2008 and October 2009, SARAO had engaged in pre-opening activity -- specifically, entering orders and then canceling them -- that \"appeared to have a significant impact on the Indicative Opening Price.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "346" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/44aaf3028f11> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The 2010 ‘flash crash’ now has a criminal suspect" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "350" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/44c5c21f4abb> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Sarao was trading E-mini S&P 500 futures contracts, but he wanted a more convenient way to \"not to trade them\", so he e-mailed his FCM (futures commission merchant, i.e. broker) for help automating that." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "346" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4d1c5e804529> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Navinder Sarao: The man accused of causing the US market to crash" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "363" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4d8f85ff8463> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[363] He was operating on the Chicago Mercantile Exchange, a highly computerised market where normal human beings stand little chance." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "363" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/52d3913171e8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[370] A single selling order of an enormously large amount of E-Mini S&P contracts and subsequent aggressive selling orders executed by high-frequency algorithms triggered the massive decline in market prices." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "370" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/56f3f9253d7c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Sarao began his alleged market manipulation in 2009 with commercially available trading software whose code he modified \"so he could rapidly place and cancel orders automatically.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "345" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5bd9d919c217> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The 2010 Flash Crash: What Caused It and How to Prevent the Next One" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "366" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6105f8973c53> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[345] As recently as May 2014, a CFTC report concluded that high-frequency traders \"did not cause the Flash Crash, but contributed to it by demanding immediacy ahead of other market participants.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "345" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6284b827ffec> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A single selling order of an enormously large amount of E-Mini S&P contracts and subsequent aggressive selling orders executed by high-frequency algorithms triggered the massive decline in market prices." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "370" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6c20e81e5bc9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "2010 Flash Crash" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "345" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6d9055cc6ffd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "U.S. District Judge Andrea Wood has issued an order freezing and preserving assets under Mr. Sarao and his firm’s control." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "365" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6f82bc57af4c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "What Really Caused the Flash Crash" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "369" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/86aa0b307c73> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Commodity Futures Trading Commission also filed civil charges against Navinder Singh Sarao and his company." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "350" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8dd9b074b87c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "2010 Flash Crash" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "370" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/94b55694f6fc> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Justice Department on Tuesday unsealed charges, and sought extradition, of a Brit who conducted day trading in futures contracts from his London home." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "350" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a1a6f71f011e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Commodity Futures Trading Commission (CFTC) investigation concluded that Sarao \"was at least significantly responsible for the order imbalances\" in the derivatives market which affected stock markets and exacerbated the flash crash." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "345" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a373d56caf93> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "iShares believes that all exchanges must agree on a standard definition to stop the next flash crash." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "366" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a43b17499f99> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "“Today’s actions make clear that the CFTC, working with its partners on the criminal side, will find and prosecute manipulators of U.S. futures markets wherever they may be,” CFTC Director of Enforcement Aitan Goelman said." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "365" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a498dadc65b2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[363] According to the FBI's investigators, Nav Sarao had modified a commercially available piece of software - a trading algorithm, to do just that." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "363" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a5a1c7decff8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[363] According to the FBI's investigators, Nav Sarao had modified a commercially available piece of software - a trading algorithm, to do just that." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "363" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a8d030d7f971> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It's classic spoofing: He'd place a lot of big orders to sell, everyone else would say, \"Ooh look at all those big sell orders, I'd better sell too,\" they'd sell, the market would go down, he'd buy, he'd turn off his algorithm, everyone else would say, \"Oh hey never mind, things are great again, there are no more big sell orders,\" they'd buy, the price would go back up, and Sarao would sell the futures he'd bought at a lower price a moment ago." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "346" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/af35a64a2b81> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "But not iShares, the Blackrock ( BLK ) subsidiary that accounts for 50% of trading in exchange-traded funds (ETFs)." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "366" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b1433f49d94d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Located in Overland Park, Kansas, Waddell & Reed was (and is) one of the oldest mutual fund companies in America." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "348" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c80fe25655a9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "But the E-mini trades that the agencies said triggered the big moves were from a large trader, subsequently identified as Waddell & Reed." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "350" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c9f04f2db249> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[345] On April 21, 2015... the U.S. Department of Justice laid '22 criminal counts, including fraud and market manipulation' against Navinder Singh Sarao, a trader." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "345" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ce3cd6543f48> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[366] By 2010, a mere 15% to 17% of all NYSE trades were controlled by the NYSE (the new electronic exchanges controlled the rest)." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "366" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e2a6116b42ad> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Among the charges included was the use of spoofing algorithms; just prior to the Flash Crash, he placed thousands of E-mini S&P 500 stock index futures contracts which he planned on canceling later." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "345" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e3c5104ec47d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "As it turns, high-frequency trading algorithms were driving the bids on dozens of ETFs and other stocks as low as one penny per share." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "364" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e4ff5754da94> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Using that software and at high speed, they alleged, he was placing big sell orders, sometimes amounting to hundreds of millions of dollars a day - trades with which he never intended to go through." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "363" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e876690737f4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Navinder Singh Sarao was eventually convicted for his role in the 2010 flash crash, as he used a spoofing algorithm to cause the crash." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "364" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ef4af3078ae4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Why the Cause of the 2010 Stock Market Flash Crash Really Matters" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "348" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/effe49f61141> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "How an Indian-origin trader caused the 2010 ‘flash crash’" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "365" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f560061d3faf> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Top 3 Financial Crashes Caused by High-frequency Trading Algorithms" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "364" .

